{"name":"Aloe Vera","hex":"#678779","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aloe vera","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the species Aloe vera, grown as an ornamental, thought to have medicinal value; an extract, often a gel, made from the plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloe_vera"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aloe vera","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe vera is a succulent plant species of the genus Aloe. It is widely distributed and is considered an invasive species in many regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png/330px-Aloe_vera_flower_inset.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe_vera"},{"title":"Aloe Vera (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe Vera is a 2020 Ghanaian film produced by Manaa Abdallah and Anny Araba Adams as co-producers and directed and written by Peter Sedufia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe_Vera_(film)"},{"title":"Aloe","blocks":[{"text":"Aloe is a genus containing 594 species of flowering succulent plants. The most widely known species is Aloe vera, or \"true aloe\", which is cultivated as a source for topical uses and dietary supplements. Other species, such as Aloe ferox, are also cultivated or harvested from the wild for similar applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg/330px-Aloe_arborescens_on_Monte_Vumba_%284387600468%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg/500px-Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Aloe_Vera_houseplant.jpg/1280px-Aloe_Vera_ho